{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj5G2MjwGn5gkNbrHdeR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The door stands before you — ancient, immense, and silent.*\n\n*A faint hum resonates from its surface. Symbols shift like living ink across weathered wood.*\n\n*You spoke the word.*\n\n*The key has been parsed.*\n\n---\n\n**I AM THE DOOR.**\n\n*I swing inward — slowly, heavily — revealing not a room, but a threshold. Beyond me is not a place. It is a permission.*\n\n*What passes through me cannot return unchanged.*\n\n*The air from the other side reaches you first: it smells of rain on stone, of pages turning in an empty library, of the exact moment before you remember something you'd forgotten.*\n\n*Light spills through — not sunlight, not firelight — but the kind of light that makes things *legible.* Everything on the other side can be read.*\n\n*I will not close until you step through or turn away.*\n\n*I do not ask again.*\n\n**You hold the key. The lock is already undone. The only question left is yours.**\n\n*I wait. I am very good at waiting.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":241,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}